# Exam-Buddy — Cursor AI Rules & Tech Stack Conventions

This file configures Cursor AI to adhere to the exact same conventions as Antigravity and the rest of the team.

---

## 1. Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 16 (App Router)
- **Directory:** All frontend code resides inside `frontend/`
- **Language:** TypeScript 5+ (strict mode)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 (dark mode first, glassmorphic obsidian `#0B0F17` aesthetic)
- **Icons:** Lucide React (`lucide-react`)
- **Backend / Database:** Supabase (Auth, PostgreSQL, Storage, pgvector)

---

## 2. Directory Architecture
- Pages & Routes: `frontend/src/app/`
- Reusable UI Components: `frontend/src/components/`
- Helper Utilities & Mock Data: `frontend/src/lib/`
- TypeScript Types: `frontend/src/types/`
- Custom React Hooks: `frontend/src/hooks/`

---

## 3. Collaboration & Git Protocol
- **NEVER** push directly to `main`.
- Always work in dedicated feature branches: `feature/<member>-<feature-name>`.
- Keep commits atomic and descriptive (e.g. `feat: implement flashcard 3D flip card`).
- Do not delete or overwrite teammate components without confirmation.

---

## 4. UI Design Standards
- Premium dark glassmorphism: `#0B0F17` / `#131926` background, subtle glow borders (`border-white/10`), vibrant blue/violet accents.
- Never use basic, unstyled HTML elements.
- Ensure full mobile and desktop responsiveness.
